  "portability_changes": [
    "Package-relative backend and decoder architecture imports; no original workspace code directory required.",
    "Public JSON configuration, inference-only condition preparation and Base/Fast generation interfaces.",
    "Source deployment operators and W2 clock retained; removed unused Monarch dependency and private encoder loader.",
    "Source sampling loop exposed as a streaming iterator with delivery before clean KV commit.",
    "Tensor-only VAE packages use config/weight checksums rather than requiring Python in the weight directory.",
    "Internal backend namespace renamed to lynnreal_core; original source attribution and legal records retained in acknowledgements. Tensor names, shapes and inference schedules are preserved.",
    "Extracted inference-only packing, schedules and model invocation; removed training objectives/replay and all non-H3 backends.",
    "Fast inference loads a sampling-specialized transformer with streaming time conditioning; reference and accelerated paths use the same exported weights.",
    "Pinned public Transformers 5.14.1 and Diffusers 0.40.0 after real GPU preparation exposed an incompatible Qwen API in 4.57.x.",
    "Pinned public FA3 source build helper and anonymous, scoped downloads; matching hand encoder included in Fast.",
    "Portable downloaded inference recipes and model indexes are supported without replacing checked-in configs.",
    "FA3 startup gradient verification explicitly leaves outer inference mode, then restores the caller context.",
    "Exact block kernels are installed before streaming attention, matching the source single-H200 engine.",
    "FA3 build enables both DiT BF16/128 and decoder FP16/64; installation smoke-tests both profiles when CUDA is available.",
    "Complete model snapshots can resolve bundled official conditioning components and the Fast decoder locally.",
    "Compact inference exports load sampling-specific AdaLN modulation tables directly and omit learned block projections; original export sources are read-only.",
    "Use stable inference module names for H3 components, fused kernels, and Ultra-Fast-VAE; retain serialized model formats and numerical operations.",
    "Remove an unused private query-fusion hook; retain native query normalization and exact rotary dispatch in streaming attention.",
    "Native 1344x768 Fast inference reuses the released 768p Ultra-Fast-VAE interface and derives packed sampler geometry from cache dimensions; the 540p default and sampling schedule are retained."
  ],
